# Intentionally empty of directives (2026-08-06). The real host
# overrides moved to fragments/i3sec-hosts.server - CoreDNS only
# allows one `hosts` plugin instance per server block, and k3s's stock
# `.:53` block already has one (NodeHosts), so a second `hosts {}`
# spliced in here via *.override fails to start ("this plugin can only
# be used once per Server Block"). This file is kept (rather than
# deleted) only because k3s's own Corefile does
# `import /etc/coredns/custom/*.override` unconditionally - as long as
# CoreDNS tolerates a zero-directive match, an empty file here is
# simpler than adding conditional logic. If CoreDNS ever needs this
# glob to match nothing at all, delete this file instead.
